 "result": "I created three files in the repository root and left existing files untouched. I could not build or run the image here, so the Dockerfile is verified by reading the code only.\n\nFiles created:\n- `Dockerfile`\n- `.dockerignore`\n- `scripts/entrypoint.sh`\n\nThe Dockerfile has three stages. It builds the Next.js admin UI as a static export and copies it to `/app/web_dist`, which is where FastAPI serves it from. It installs Python dependencies with `uv sync --frozen` from `uv.lock`. The runtime stage is `python:3.13-slim` with Chromium, Node, git, and openssl, and it runs under tini. The entrypoint starts the Grok Browser Bridge, waits for its `/health`, then runs `python main.py`. The bridge is optional, so the app still starts if it fails.\n\nChoices you may want to change:\n- **Runs as root.** The app listens on port 83, which needs root or a capability.\n- **Port and data:** `PORT=83` and `/app/data` are the defaults. `LOGIN_SECRET` is not set in the image, so pass it at runtime. The code falls back to `admin` otherwise.\n- **`scripts/entrypoint.sh` is new.** The technical guide references it, but it wasn't in the repo.\n- **Node version:** the bridge uses Debian's `nodejs` package, not the Node 22 image the guide describes. The frontend build does use `node:22-alpine`.\n- **uv pinned to 0.8.17.** I picked this version without checking the registry, so confirm the tag exists.\n\nThings to check on the first build:\n- The Debian package names (`chromium`, `nodejs`, `npm`, `tini`) and the Alpine frontend build.\n- `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` point at the Aliyun PyPI mirror, so the build must be able to reach it.",
